{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Thus</b> — The priests are the teachers of the Torah, and in the days of Haggai they would offer burnt offerings on the altar for nineteen years before the House was built, and in the book of Daniel this is explained explicitly. And now Joshua was included among the priests, he being the high priest, and they would seek Torah from his mouth, and he would not err in answering. And we have seen, according to the peshat, that Haggai did not say to the priests that they had not taught Torah truly; rather he said this about this people."], :book :haggai, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Haggai" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/hagai"] ["Ibn Ezra on Haggai -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/hagai"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:49:30.869237204Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}